<title>YUGOSLAVIA: SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT YUGOSLAVIA 2-1 IN U-21 EUROPEAN QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT YUGOSLAVIA 2-1 IN U-21 EUROPEAN QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>NOVI SAD, Yugoslavia 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia lost</p>
<p>1-2 to Spain (halftime 0-1) in an under-21 European soccer</p>
<p>championship group six qualifier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Yugoslavia - Mihajlo Pjanovic 53</p>
<p>Spain - Roger Garcia 20 pen, Jose Moreno 50</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>    Standings   P  W  D  L   F  A  Pts</p>
<p> Spain	    6  5  1  0  10  3   16</p>
<p> Yugoslavia     5  3  0  2   6  3    9</p>
<p> Slovakia	 3  2  1  0  10  1    7</p>
<p> Czech Republic 4  1  0  3   7  6    3</p>
<p> Malta	    6  0  0  6   0 21    0</p>
</text>
